  - nodeId: 5
    spanishLine: El tren ________ (venir) a la plataforma cuatro y ________ (salir)
      en dos minutos
    englishHint: 'The train is a he according to Spanish Grammar rules and we are
      only talking about one train. In this case we are using simple future tense
      because the train hasn''t come but will come. Likewise it hasn''t left but
      it will leave. Venir: Yo(I) - Vendre, Tu(You) - Vendras, El/Ella/Usted(He/She/You(Formal))
      - Vendra, Nosotros(We) -  Vendremos, Ellos/Ellas/Ustedes (They/Them/You All)
      - Vendran. Salir: Yo(I) - Saldre, Tu(You) - Saldras, El/Ella/Usted(He/She/You
      (Formal) -  Saldra, Nosotros(We) - Saldremos, Ellos/Ellas/Ustedes (They/Them/You
      All) - Saldran '
    options:
    - responseText: Vendre, Saldre
      nextNodeId: 5
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Vendras, Saldras
      nextNodeId: 5
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Vendra, Saldra
      nextNodeId: 6
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Vendremos, Saldremos
      nextNodeId: 5
      endsConversation: 0
    - responseText: Vendran, Saldran
      nextNodeId: 5
      endsConversation: 0
  - nodeId: 6
    spanishLine: "\xA1Las puertas se abren! Yo ________ ________ (ir + a + subir)
